                    "Iron Ore [लौह अयस्क] in India is predominantly high-grade Haematite (60-70% Fe) and Magnetite (black ore); Odisha is the leading producer (Barabil-Koira valley, Badampahar, Gorumahisani in Mayurbhanj).",
