                    "Tarapur Atomic Power Station [तारापुर] in Maharashtra (commissioned in 1969 with American Boiling Water Reactors) was India's first commercial nuclear power station.",
                    "Narora Atomic Power Station [नरोरा परमाणु ऊर्जा संयंत्र] in Bulandshahr district, Uttar Pradesh, is the only nuclear power plant in UP, operating two indigenous 220 MW Pressurized Heavy Water Reactors (PHWR) using heavy water (D2O) as moderator and coolant from the Ganga.",
